From: GreenAutarky OS <noreply@greenautarky.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: rk3328: DSGW-210 usb20_otg as peripheral in u-boot

rk3328-rock64.dts sets &usb20_otg dr_mode = "host". The dwc2 gadget driver
(DM_USB_GADGET) rejects any node that is neither "peripheral" nor "otg", so
rockusb would fail with "No USB device found". On the DSGW-210 this controller
is the USB-C port (the kernel runs it as a CDC-ACM gadget), and in u-boot it
is only ever used as a gadget: set dr_mode = "peripheral" in the u-boot dtsi.
The kernel DT is not affected (it is built from board/dusun/dsgw210/dts).

Applies on top of 0001-relabel-as-dsgw210.patch.

Signed-off-by: GreenAutarky OS <noreply@greenautarky.invalid>
---
--- a/arch/arm/dts/rk3328-rock64-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3328-rock64-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -67,6 +67,13 @@
 
 &usb20_otg {
 	hnp-srp-disable;
+	/*
+	 * DSGW-210: the USB-C port is the device port. rock64 sets
+	 * dr_mode = "host", which makes the dwc2 gadget driver refuse the
+	 * controller ("Invalid mode"), so no rockusb. Peripheral mode lets
+	 * u-boot serve rockusb (2207:320c) here for re-flashing over USB-C.
+	 */
+	dr_mode = "peripheral";
 };
 
 &vcc_sd {
